// `*` has no bare form; importing it bare is a parse error whose message says
// to import the builtin aliased (`wrapping_mul as *`).
import { * } from builtins;

fn main() -> i64 { 6 * 7 }
--- errors ---
error: an operator has no bare import: import the builtin it stands for and alias it to the operator, e.g. `wrapping_add as +`
 --> ./tests/cases/arithmetic/err_bare_star.aipl:3:10
  |
3 | import { * } from builtins;
  |          ^
